  "home_vero_eyebrow": "A real draw, not an animation",
  "home_vero_titolo": "Every card you touch is a real card.",
  "home_vero_testo": "When the deck moves, when you cut it, when you choose from the fan, you are not watching a graphic effect. On the table lies a real deck of virtual cards — the full 78, or the 22 Major Arcana — each with its own identity and its own orientation, like the cards in your hands.",
  "home_vero_fatti_0_titolo": "Shuffled by chance",
  "home_vero_fatti_0_testo": "The order comes from a cryptographic source of randomness, not from a script. No one decides it in advance — not even us. You decide when the shuffle ends.",
  "home_vero_fatti_1_titolo": "Cut where you choose",
  "home_vero_fatti_1_testo": "The point you touch is where the real deck divides: the cards after it move to the front, as they would between your hands.",
  "home_vero_fatti_2_titolo": "Sealed before you draw",
  "home_vero_fatti_2_testo": "Before the fan opens, every card already holds its place, sealed with a cryptographic fingerprint. The card you touch is the card you draw — and at the end you can verify that nothing changed.",
  "home_vero_chiusa": "A draw as honest as one made live, at a table. What the cards say remains a matter of reflection, never a guaranteed prediction.",
  "home_memoria_citazione": "“Last week you asked how your relationship might develop. How are things going now?”",
  "home_memoria_piede": "A follow-up begins with what matters, not a blank page.",
  "home_memoria_eyebrow": "Your reader remembers your story",
  "home_memoria_titolo": "Continuity without pretending to know more than you share.",
